// EXPECT: PASS
// README "Contextual Extension": "Make changes that are only seen from
// the point of view (the Context) of the place where the object was
// re-opened. From other places, the object will still appear
// unchanged." Widget is found only by ascending from German (not
// German's own child), so reopening it with a block is contextual -
// Size only exists on German's own extension of Widget, not on the
// real, global Widget.
Widget: {
	Colour: String;
}
German: {
	Widget {
		Size: String;
	}
}

// Confirmed by hand (ADL_DEBUG=1): the real TOP.Widget still has only
// Colour as a direct child; Size lives on an anonymous extension
// (aspect=German) parented *on* Widget itself, findable only by
// ascending from within German's own context, not from TOP.

// A plain reopen of the *same* Widget from TOP's own scope - not
// ascended, so not contextual - adds a real, globally-visible field.
Widget {
	Weight: String;
}
